## Key Design Decisions

| Concern | Handling |
|---|---|
| **Existing query string** | Merged via `URLSearchParams` instead of overwritten. |
| **Hash fragments** | Preserved and appended after the query string. |
| **Arrays** | Repeated key (`tags=red&tags=blue`) — the most widely-compatible format. |
| **`null` / `undefined`** | Skipped entirely (common REST convention). |
| **Empty string / `0` / `false`** | Kept — these are valid values. |
| **Encoding** | Delegated to `URLSearchParams`, which uses `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` rules. |
| **Dates** | Serialized as ISO 8601 strings. |

If you prefer comma-joined arrays (`tags=red,blue`) instead of repeated keys, replace the array branch with:

