// → "https://api.example.com/search?q=cats&page=2&tags=a&tags=b"

buildUrl('/users', { id: 5 });
// → "/users?id=5"
```

Notes:
- Values are automatically URL-encoded (spaces become `+`, special characters are escaped).
- `null`/`undefined` values are skipped, so you can pass optional parameters directly.
- Arrays produce repeated keys (`?tag=a&tag=b`).
- If you want arrays as comma-separated values instead, replace the array branch with `search.append(key, value.join(','))`.

