- **Spaces**: `URLSearchParams` encodes a space as `+` (form-encoding). If you need `%20` instead, decode it back: `search.toString().replace(/\+/g, '%20')`.
- **Arrays**: this implementation repeats the key (`tags=a&tags=b`). If your API expects `tags[]=a&tags[]=b`, change the array branch to `search.append(`${name}[]`, toValue(item))`.
- **Boolean params**: `false` is kept as `false`. If your API expects booleans to be omitted when false, add `if (value === false) continue;` in the scalar branch.

